---
---
<section class="nx-section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--nx-border);">
  <div class="nx-section-inner">
    <h2 class="nx-section-title">Security by isolation.</h2>
    <p class="nx-section-sub">
      Actor patterns eliminate entire classes of vulnerability. Type checking enforces the contract.
    </p>

    <div class="sh-grid">
      <div class="sh-card">
        <span class="sh-label">isolation</span>
        <h3 class="sh-title">No shared mutable state</h3>
        <p class="sh-body">
          Actors cannot corrupt each other's data. TOCTOU races and data races
          are removed at the language level — not by convention.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sh-card">
        <span class="sh-label">mailboxes</span>
        <h3 class="sh-title">Explicit overflow policy</h3>
        <p class="sh-body">
          Mailbox capacity and overflow strategy are explicit configuration.
          DoS-by-flooding becomes a tunable policy decision, not an incident.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sh-card">
        <span class="sh-label">persistence</span>
        <h3 class="sh-title">Single-writer guarantee</h3>
        <p class="sh-body">
          Each ActorSystem owns a unique ULID. Persistence stores reject foreign
          writes. Split-brain corruption cannot happen silently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sh-card">
        <span class="sh-label">tooling</span>
        <h3 class="sh-title">Verified by Psalm</h3>
        <p class="sh-body">
          Custom Psalm rules enforce readonly messages and immutable actor state.
          Security invariants are checked at analysis time, not runtime.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-cta">
      <a href="/security" class="sh-link">→ Read the full security model</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .nx-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .nx-section-inner {
    max-width: 1152px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .nx-section-title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--nx-text);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .nx-section-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--nx-text-muted);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .sh-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .sh-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .sh-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .sh-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--nx-border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--nx-bg-raised);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .sh-label {
    font-family: var(--nx-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--nx-accent);
  }

  .sh-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--nx-text);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .sh-body {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--nx-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sh-cta {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sh-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--nx-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--nx-border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .sh-link:hover {
    background: var(--nx-bg-raised);
    color: var(--nx-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
